[% PageVersion = 'Documentation/changelog/2026-08-10-openrouter-pricing-feed.tt,v 1.00 2026/08/10 shanta Exp' %]
[% IF c.session.debug_mode == 1 %][% PageVersion %][% END %]

[% META title = 'OpenRouter Pricing Feed &mdash; Keep per-token cost from /api/v1/models' %]
[% META description = 'Provider::OpenRouter::list_models now keeps the pricing hash instead of discarding it; cost flows through the Router into ModelCatalog as price_prompt, price_completion and a threshold-derived price_tier' %]
[% META author = 'shanta' %]
[% META date = '2026-08-10' %]
[% META roles = 'admin developer' %]

<div class="changelog-entry">
    <header class="changelog-header">
        <h1>OpenRouter Pricing Feed &mdash; Keep per-token cost</h1>
        <div class="changelog-meta">
            <span class="date">August 10, 2026</span>
            <span class="author">by shanta</span>
            <span class="type">Feature / AIMPS-P1 (#253)</span>
        </div>
    </header>

    <section class="changelog-summary">
        <h2>Summary</h2>
        <p>
            <code>Provider::OpenRouter::list_models</code> previously mapped each model to
            only <code>{ id, label }</code> and threw away the <code>pricing</code> object
            that OpenRouter returns from <code>/api/v1/models</code>. The real per-token
            cost is now kept and carried all the way through to the shared model catalog,
            so every AI surface can sort, filter and display by actual price. This
            completes Phase 1 of
            <a href="[% c.uri_for('/Documentation/AIModelPresentationPlan') %]">AI Model
            Presentation &amp; Selection</a> (project 252, sub-project 253).
        </p>
    </section>

    <section class="changelog-details">
        <h2>What changed</h2>
        <ul>
            <li><strong><code>Provider::OpenRouter::list_models</code></strong> now keeps the
                raw <code>pricing</code> hash and adds <code>price_prompt</code> and
                <code>price_completion</code> as USD-per-1M-token numbers. OpenRouter reports
                per-token prices as strings (<code>"0.000001"</code>); the new
                <code>_per_million</code> helper converts them to per-1M USD and returns
                <code>0</code> for anything missing or non-numeric.</li>
            <li><strong><code>Model::AI2::Router::get_available_models</code></strong> carries
                <code>pricing</code>, <code>price_prompt</code> and
                <code>price_completion</code> on each OpenRouter model it emits (the
                <code>:free</code> slugs carry a zero pricing hash).</li>
            <li><strong><code>Model::Util::ModelCatalog::_flatten</code></strong> exposes
                <code>price_prompt</code>, <code>price_completion</code> and a new
                <code>price_tier</code> on every catalog entry. The tier is
                <strong>threshold-derived</strong> (never a hardcoded model list, which
                would rot as the catalog changes weekly):
                <ul>
                    <li><code>free</code> &mdash; zero per-token cost</li>
                    <li><code>cheap</code> &mdash; dearer side &le; $1 / 1M tokens</li>
                    <li><code>mid</code> &mdash; dearer side &le; $5 / 1M tokens</li>
                    <li><code>premium</code> &mdash; dearer side &gt; $5 / 1M tokens</li>
                </ul>
                Tiers are ranked by the dearer of prompt/completion so a model is not
                under-classified when only its output price is high.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Verified</h2>
        <p>
            All three modules pass <code>perl -c</code>. A standalone harness fed sample
            OpenRouter pricing through the real <code>_flatten</code> /
            <code>_price_tier</code> path and produced the expected tiers:
            <code>:free</code> &rarr; <code>free</code>; Gemini 2.0 Flash ($0.1/$0.4 per 1M)
            &rarr; <code>cheap</code>; GPT-4.1 ($2/$8), Claude 3.5 Sonnet ($3/$15) and
            GPT-4o ($5/$15) &rarr; <code>premium</code>; Ollama &rarr; <code>local</code>
            (tier <code>free</code>, no cash cost).
        </p>

        <h2>Follow-up (phases 2&ndash;5)</h2>
        <p>
            Phases 2&ndash;5 (cost-aware sorting/filtering/price display, page- and
            role-scoped shortlists, usage telemetry, and the standing v2-migration /
            documentation-sync rules) remain tracked in the
            <a href="[% c.uri_for('/Documentation/AIModelPresentationPlan') %]">AIMPS plan</a>
            (todos 2023&ndash;2035).
        </p>

        <h2>Follow-up fix (same day): <code>/ai2/providers</code> was stripping pricing</h2>
        <p>
            After P1 landed, the model dropdown still showed the provider (optgroup
            header) but a <strong>blank fee</strong> on every option &mdash; not a browser
            cache issue. Root cause: <code>Controller::AI2::providers</code> rebuilt each
            catalog model as only <code>{ id, label, unreachable }</code> and dropped the
            <code>price_*</code> / <code>pricing</code> fields before calling
            <code>ModelCatalog->prime()</code>, so the shared cache was primed with
            price-less entries and every surface that reads it rendered no cost.
            Fixed by passing <code>price_prompt</code> / <code>price_completion</code> /
            <code>pricing</code> / <code>local</code> through in the <code>providers</code>
            endpoint. Verified live: <code>/ai2/providers</code> returned 399/414 priced
            models and <code>/ai/widget</code> now renders
            <code>AI21: Jamba Large 1.7 &mdash; $2.00/$8.00 per 1M (premium)</code>,
            <code>Ollama &mdash; local</code>, <code>:free &mdash; free</code>, etc.
        </p>

        <h2>Files changed</h2>
        <ul>
            <li><code>lib/Comserv/Model/AI2/Provider/OpenRouter.pm</code> &mdash; keep pricing, add <code>_per_million</code></li>
            <li><code>lib/Comserv/Model/AI2/Router.pm</code> &mdash; carry pricing through <code>get_available_models</code></li>
            <li><code>lib/Comserv/Util/ModelCatalog.pm</code> &mdash; expose <code>price_prompt</code> / <code>price_completion</code> / <code>price_tier</code></li>
            <li><code>lib/Comserv/Controller/AI2.pm</code> &mdash; stop stripping pricing in <code>providers</code> (pass <code>price_*</code> / <code>pricing</code> / <code>local</code> through)</li>
            <li><code>root/Documentation/AIModelPresentationPlan.tt</code> &mdash; mark P1 delivered</li>
            <li><code>root/Documentation/changelog/2026-08-10-openrouter-pricing-feed.tt</code> &mdash; this entry</li>
        </ul>
    </section>
</div>
